Select the agent's bridge for the application's opentelemetry-api.

The application's opentelemetry-api is a separate copy from the vendored one. It loads its runtime
context (OTEL_PYTHON_CONTEXT) and tracer provider (OTEL_PYTHON_TRACER_PROVIDER) from entry points,
and the opentelemetry-agent distribution registers the bridge (opentelemetry.agent._bridge) under the
name _AGENT_BRIDGE. The bridge shares the vendored context and delegates to the vendored tracer
provider. sitecustomize sets both variables unless they're already set.

The vendored API reads the same variables but only sees the vendored distributions' entry points
(see otel-importlib-metadata.patch), so it treats _AGENT_BRIDGE as unset: it uses its default runtime
context, which the bridge is built on, and its global tracer provider, which the bridge delegates to.

